{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1792600868","published":"2026-10-21T17:11:00Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:32:02.718228852Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-19385"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-19385","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: Out-of-bounds read in pg_dump on long protrftypes.\n     dumpFunc() parsed pg_proc.protrftypes into a fixed FUNC_MAX_ARGS\n     array that is not zero-terminated when the server reports exactly\n     FUNC_MAX_ARGS entries, so the TRANSFORM loop read past the buffer;\n     a function with more entries made pg_dump abort.  Any role that can\n     create functions in a language with a transform could thus break or\n     corrupt dumps.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-19385.patch: make parseOidArray() allocate\n       the array itself (exact count, or input-sized and zero-terminated),\n       add parseIntArray() for pg_index.indkey, and use them in\n       getAggregates(), getFuncs(), getIndexes() and dumpFunc(); add a\n       function with a transform to the object_address regression test\n       (upstream 57aa21f691; older-server branches of 9.5 pg_dump kept).\n     - CVE-2026-19385","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libecpg-compat3","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libecpg-compat3?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.5.25-0ubuntu0.16.04.1+tuxcare.els15"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu16.04els/CLSA-2026-1792600868.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libecpg-dev","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libecpg-dev?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"9.5.25-0ubuntu0.16.04.1+tuxcare.els15"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu16.04els/CLSA-2026-1792600868.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libecpg6","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libecpg6